  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Private Sector Development Capacity Building IDF Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">On June 28, 2012 the World Bank had received a formal request for assistance from the Kyrgyz Republic, requesting technical and financial Assistance in capacity strengthening and implementation of Strategy for Private Sector Development in the Kyrgyz Republic.  As response to this request, the team would like to prepare and IDF proposal which would aim to support the new government of Kyrgyzstan in building capacity to develop and implement PSD policy/strategy and business environment agenda.   The key objectives of the capacity building activities would encompass: &#x2022;  Supporting and strengthening the capacity of public bodies in developing and implementing the policy of private sector development through building up the capacity to perform analysis, and prioritizing proposed interventions; &#x2022;  Strengthening the interagency coordination between key governmental bodies that are in charge of economic policy, in order to guide the process of decision making in private sector development; &#x2022;  Assisting the Government in improving coordination, communication and organization of the agreed strategy, in order to mobilize donor support for business environment improvement; and &#x2022;  Carrying out the necessary studies and implementing the actions specified in the Private Sector Development Strategy.</narrative>
  </description>
